      "text": "To determine the perimeter of triangle \\(XYZ\\), we first need to find the coordinates of points \\(X\\), \\(Y\\), and \\(Z\\).\n\nThe base \\(ABC\\) of the prism is an equilateral triangle with side length 12. Therefore, we can place the vertices of the base as follows:\n- \\(A = (0, 0)\\)\n- \\(B = (12, 0)\\)\n- \\(C = (6, -6)\\)\n\nThe height of the prism is 16 units. Points \\(X\\), \\(Y\\), and \\(Z\\) are the midpoints of edges \\(AC\\), \\(BC\\), and \\(DC\\) respectively. We can find these coordinates as follows:\n- \\(X\\) is the midpoint of \\(AC\\):\n  \\[\n  X = \\left( \\frac{0+6}{2}, \\frac{0-6}{2} \\right) = (3, -3)\n  \\]\n- \\(Y\\) is the midpoint of \\(BC\\):\n  \\[\n  Y = \\left( \\frac{12+6}{2}, \\frac{0-6}{2} \\right) = (9, -3)\n  \\]\n- \\(Z\\) is the midpoint of \\(DC\\):\n  \\[\n  Z = \\left( \\frac{12+6}{2}, \\frac{0-22}{2} \\right) = (9, -11)\n  \\]\n\nNow, we need to find the lengths of the sides of triangle \\(XYZ\\):\n- The distance \\(XY\\) is:\n  \\[\n  XY = \\sqrt{(9-3)^2 + (-3+3)^2} = \\sqrt{6^2 + 0^2} = 6\n  \\]\n- The distance \\(YZ\\) is:\n  \\[\n  YZ = \\sqrt{(9-9)^2 + (-11+3)^2} = \\sqrt{0^2 + (-8)^2} = 8\n  \\]\n- The distance \\(XZ\\) is:\n  \\[\n  XZ = \\sqrt{(9-3)^2 + (-3+11)^2} = \\sqrt{6^2 + 8^2} = \\sqrt{36 + 64} = \\sqrt{100} = 10\n  \\]\n\nThe perimeter of triangle \\(XYZ\\) is the sum of the lengths of its sides:\n\\[\nXY + YZ + XZ = 6 + 8 + 10 = 24\n\\]\n\nThus, the perimeter of triangle \\(XYZ\\) is \\(\\boxed{24}\\).",
