      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to find the perimeter of triangle \\(XYZ\\), where \\(X\\), \\(Y\\), and \\(Z\\) are the midpoints of edges \\(AC\\), \\(BC\\), and \\(DC\\) respectively in a right prism with height 16 and equilateral triangle bases of side length 12.\n\nFirst, let's identify the coordinates of the points in the prism. Assume the base of the prism is placed in the \\(xy\\)-plane with vertex \\(A\\) at \\((6, \\sqrt{144-36}) = (6, 6)\\), vertex \\(B\\) at \\((12, 6)\\), vertex \\(C\\) at \\((6, -6)\\), vertex \\(D\\) at \\((6, -22)\\), vertex \\(E\\) at \\((0, -16)\\), and vertex \\(F\\) at \\((12, -16)\\).\n\nThe midpoints \\(X\\), \\(Y\\), and \\(Z\\) are:\n- \\(X\\) is the midpoint of \\(AC\\), so \\(X = \\left( \\frac{6+6}{2}, \\frac{6-6}{2} \\right) = (6, 0)\\).\n- \\(Y\\) is the midpoint of \\(BC\\), so \\(Y = \\left( \\frac{12+6}{2}, \\frac{6-6}{2} \\right) = (9, 0)\\).\n- \\(Z\\) is the midpoint of \\(DC\\), so \\(Z = \\left( \\frac{6+6}{2}, \\frac{-6-22}{2} \\right) = (6, -14)\\).\n\nNow, we need to find the lengths of the sides of triangle \\(XYZ\\) using the distance formula \\(d = \\sqrt{(x_2 - x_1)^2 + (y_2 - y_1)^2}\\).\n\nThe distance \\(XZ\\) is:\n\\[\nXZ = \\sqrt{(6-6)^2 + (-14-0)^2} = \\sqrt{0 + 196} = 14.\n\\]\n\nThe distance \\(YZ\\) is:\n\\[\nYZ = \\sqrt{(9-6)^2 + (0+14)^2} = \\sqrt{3^2 + 14^2} = \\sqrt{9 + 196} = \\sqrt{205}.\n\\]\n\nThe distance \\(XY\\) is:\n\\[\nXY = \\sqrt{(9-6)^2 + (0-0)^2} = \\sqrt{3^2 + 0} = \\sqrt{9} = 3.\n\\]\n\nThe perimeter of triangle \\(XYZ\\) is the sum of the lengths of its sides:\n\\[\nXY + YZ + XZ = 3 + \\sqrt{205} + 14 = 17 + \\sqrt{205}.\n\\]\n\nThus, the perimeter of triangle \\(XYZ\\) is \\(\\boxed{17 + \\sqrt{205}}\\).",
